// @run
// @log 1
// @log 10
// @log 2
// @log zz
// @log 1
// THE FIELD-TABLE PASS IS THE ONLY COLLECTOR AN INLINE-SHAPE MAP FIELD HAS —
// both halves of what it collects, isolated so each is a real pin.
//
// An INLINE shape annotation is ONE `TypeRef` name (`{m:{[i32]:i32},n:i32}`), so
// its map never reaches `collectA`'s bare-map arm the way a DECLARED
// `type S = {m: {[i32]: V}}`'s field annotation does — that one IS a standalone
// bare-map `TypeRef`. The only thing that sees this map is `collectA`'s
// FIELD-TABLE re-derivation, off the field row's own key column, and it collects
// TWO things there:
//
//   1. `mI32Used`. The flag is MODULE-WIDE and gates the i32-keyed map STRUCT
//      (`mStructI32Idx`), the `__map_probe_i32__` helper, and — the symptom — the
//      per-function 5-slot i32-KEY scratch frame (`mapI32Base`). Unset, the
//      store's key temporary aliases the map-REF temporary at the SAME local
//      index: `type mismatch: expected (ref $type), found i32`, `vl check` rc 0.
//
//   2. The mv SLOT of a REF-valued map field, interned against the i32 KEY
//      (`mvShapeOfValNameK(name, keyI32)`). Interned key-blind, the STRING-keyed
//      row is minted and the i32-keyed lookup finds nothing: `emitProgram: map
//      value type has no interned slot`.
//
// A MODULE-WIDE FLAG HIDES A MISSED SETTER THE WAY A MULTI-OP FUNCTION HIDES A
// MISSED MEMBERSHIP SCAN (#1287's lesson (a), which cost that PR its first
// sabotage) — and an INTERN is hidden the same way, by any OTHER spelling of the
// same (KEY, VALUE) pair. So this file spells the i32 key ONLY inside inline
// shapes and holds nothing else:
//   · no `const m: {[i32]: V} = Map()` binding — a bare-map `TypeRef`;
//   · no DECLARED `type S = {m: {[i32]: V}}` — its FIELD annotation is one too;
//   · no i32-keyed map in any other position.
// Sabotage `if sfk { mI32Used = true }` or the `sfk` argument beside it and this
// file fails while every other i32-keyed fixture still passes.

function mono() {
  const s: { m: {[i32]: i32}, n: i32 } = { m: Map(), n: 7 }
  s.m[11] = 3
  print(s.m.length)           // 1
  print((s.m[11] ?? 0) + s.n) // 10
  s.m[22] = 4
  print(s.m.length)           // 2
}
mono()

// The REF-valued half: the value `string` interns a per-(KEY, VALUE) mv slot, and
// this shape is the module's only mention of the i32-keyed one.
function refVal() {
  const q: { by: {[i32]: string} } = { by: Map() }
  q.by[11] = "zz"
  print(q.by[11] ?? "-")      // zz
  print(q.by.length)          // 1
}
refVal()
